## Distribution License

The licensor grants you an additional license to distribute copies of the software. Your license to distribute covers distributing the software with changes and new works permitted by [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license). You must comply with the terms of the license in everything you do with the software that would otherwise infringe the licensor's copyright in it.

## Changes and New Works License

The licensor grants you an additional license to use, copy, distribute, make changes, and make new works based on the software for any permitted purpose.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software that covers patent claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that you would infringe by using the software.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.

## Personal Uses

Personal use for research, experiment, and testing for the benefit of public knowledge, personal study, private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, or religious observance, without any anticipated commercial application, is use for a permitted purpose.

## Noncommercial Organizations

Use by charitable organizations, educational institutions, and public interest groups who are organized in a manner that does not primarily benefit the members or owners of the organization is use for a permitted purpose.

## Fair Use

You may "fair use" the software as permitted under applicable law, and that this license does not limit your fair use rights.

## Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of the software from you also gets a copy of these terms or the URL for them above.

## Excuse

You're excused for unknowingly breaking [Notices](#notices) if you take all practical steps to comply within thirty days of learning you broke the rule.

## Patent Defense

If you make written claim that Patents cover the software or that the software infringes Patents, the license granted to you ends immediately.

## Continuation

Your licenses under these terms continue through any termination, and they continue for as long as your exercise of the licensed rights is permitted under these terms.

